	affiliations = {School of Economics and Management, Weifang University of Science and Technology, Weifang, China; College of Economics and Management, Huazhong Agricultural University, Wuhan, China},
	abstract = {Digital village development serves as an essential means to comprehensively advance China’s Rural Revitalization Strategy. Investigating its impact on the income mobility of rural households is of great theoretical and practical significance. Based on fixed-observation-point data of rapeseed growers from the National Rapeseed Industry Technology System in China, this paper constructs an income transition matrix to empirically examine the impact of digital village development on rural household income mobility. The results show that digital village development significantly enhances the income mobility of rural households. In terms of direction, digital village development promotes upward income mobility among rural households. Mechanism analysis indicates that the increase in non-farm income is the primary channel through which digital village development promotes this upward mobility. Heterogeneity analysis reveals that digital village development exerts a stronger impact on the income mobility of low-income households and those with high human capital. However, for low-income households, this mobility is mainly confined within the low- and middle-income groups, making it relatively difficult to achieve a leap from a low-income to a high-income status. Copyright © 2026 Li, Li and Yuchi.},
