	abstract = {The objective of this study is to investigate intergenerational mobility in Brazil based on occupation, education, and standard of living, using a WVS (2018) database, which allowed the construction of a variable related to standard of living at an intergenerational level, not previously used for this purpose. The methodology employed was the ordered multinomial logit model, including marginal effects and heterogeneity. The results show that intergenerational education has a greater impact on raising the standard of living than occupation. It was also found that children of parents with better socioeconomic conditions tend to maintain the family standard of living. Analyses by region reveal marked differences between the Northeast and Southeast, indicating that the geographic context modulates the effects of mobility. In the Southeast, a higher probability of upward mobility was observed among individuals who surpass the occupational stratum of their parents, compared to the national average. © 2026 Lundiana. All rights reserved.},
