	affiliations = {School of Economics and Finance, South China University of Technology, Guangzhou, 510006, China},
	abstract = {Summary The essence of common prosperity is that all people create and share an increasingly better life. Narrowing the income gap and enhancing the income mobility among different groups are important ways to achieve this great goal. Against this background，measuring the Chinese residents’income mobility and investigating its dynamic evolution will help smooth the upward mobility channel and narrow the income gap of residents，which is of great significance for promoting common prosperity. The existing literature mainly adopts the two-period measurement method，but the measurement results of this method are uncertain and not conducive to observing the continuous change of income mobility from a long-term perspective. So，we adopt the contingency table method to study residents’income mobility from the perspective of multi-period measurement. This paper uses the data of ten rounds of China Health and Nutrition Survey（CHNS）to calculate the income mobility level and structure of Chinese residents，and examines their dynamic evolution process from the national，regional and micro levels. It finds that the multi-period measurement results are robust，and smoother and better than the traditional two-period measurement results. Specifically，during the measurement sample period，the income mobility level of Chinese residents showed a continuous downward trend，that is，there was a trend of income class solidification. From the grouping of different dimensions，the income mobility level of residents in urban and eastern regions was significantly lower than that of residents in rural and central and western regions，and the income mobility level of self-employed workers was much higher than that of non-self-employed workers，but there was no significant difference in different gender groups. The structure of income mobility in China was not ideal，which obviously prevented the improvement of social equality. This paper contributes to the existing literature in the following two aspects. First，in terms of methodology，the contingency table method is extended from a single horizontal dimension to a multi-dimensional measurement framework containing level and structure，which not only improves the contingency table method，but also enriches the research on residents’income mobility. Second，in terms of research content，with efforts to deliver a more detailed and in-depth study on the income mobility of Chinese residents，this paper covers two regional groups，including urban and rural areas，as well as eastern，central and western regions，and two groups concerning residents’gender and job nature，so as to further study the income mobility of Chinese residents. This paper enriches the existing research about income mobility，and confirms that the results using the contingency table method are more robust than results of the traditional two-stage measurement method. In addition，based on the measurement result，this paper suggests that in contrast to focusing on short-term income gap，more attention should be paid to enhancing the residents’income mobility level and improving the residents’income mobility structure. Specifically，the government should take targeted policy measures to improve the income increase mechanism and the fair income distribution mechanism，stimulate residents’awareness of entrepreneurship. © 2022 Editorial Board of Modern Economic Science. All rights reserved.},
